.TH SDL_GL_SetAttribute 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GL_SetAttribute \- Set an OpenGL window attribute before window creation.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GL_SetAttribute(SDL_GLAttr attr, int value);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function sets the OpenGL attribute
.BR attr
to
.BR value \[char46]
The requested attributes should be set before creating an OpenGL window\[char46] You should use
.BR SDL_GL_GetAttribute ()
to check the values after creating the OpenGL context, since the values obtained can differ from the requested ones\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I attr
an enum value specifying the OpenGL attribute to set\[char46]
.TP
.I value
the desired value for the attribute\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_GL_CreateContext (3),
.BR SDL_GL_GetAttribute (3),
.BR SDL_GL_ResetAttributes (3)
